@startuml registration_persistence
!theme cyborg
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
title When is Device registration ready? Only after the record is saved
participant COMMUNICATION
database STORAGE
participant "WIFI\n(verified TLS 1.3)" as WIFI
participant "FHIR server" as Server
COMMUNICATION -> STORAGE : boot: read fhir/device-registration once
alt Valid record for this server and physical identity
 STORAGE --> COMMUNICATION : record
 COMMUNICATION -> COMMUNICATION : registration ready from cache\n(no POST, no readback; not proof the server still holds it)
else Missing, malformed or other binding
 COMMUNICATION -> COMMUNICATION : registration needed (Idle, verified transport, gap over)
 COMMUNICATION -> WIFI : POST /Device, If-None-Exist: identifier=urn%3Astethoscope%3Adevice|stetho-AABBCCDDEEFF\nsame physical identifier every time; 10 s attempt budget
 WIFI -> Server : request
 Server --> WIFI : 201 Created or 200 OK (existing match)
 WIFI --> COMMUNICATION : status, Location, body
 COMMUNICATION -> COMMUNICATION : validate: Location base path and type, body identifier,\nids agree; else attempt failed
 note right of COMMUNICATION : HTTP 200/201 alone is not readiness
 COMMUNICATION -> COMMUNICATION : candidate Device id in memory only
 COMMUNICATION -> STORAGE : write complete record (URL, identifier, Device id)
 alt Save succeeded
  STORAGE --> COMMUNICATION : committed
  COMMUNICATION -> COMMUNICATION : publish registration ready
 else Save failed
  STORAGE --> COMMUNICATION : error; previous committed record preserved
  COMMUNICATION -> COMMUNICATION : not ready; DEVICE_REGISTRATION_FAILURE;\nnext attempt repeats only the save (same boot)
 end
end
group Lost receipt (server committed, response lost)
 Server -->x WIFI : 201 Created lost
 COMMUNICATION -> COMMUNICATION : attempt failed; after the gap repeat the conditional POST\nwith the same physical identifier
 Server --> COMMUNICATION : 200 OK for the existing Device; validate and save as above
end
note over COMMUNICATION, Server
 Failed attempt, never a fallback: 412 (multiple matches), unsupported conditional create, authentication,
 configuration or trust failure latch DEVICE_REGISTRATION_FAILURE; never an unconditional POST, never a new identity.
 Recovery: 60 s after the first failure, doubling (120, 240 s); the 4th failure leaves registration
 unavailable until restart. After a restart with no saved record the conditional POST is repeated.
 Atomicity and power-loss behavior of the save remain target evidence.
end note
@enduml
